WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
A healthy install, with nothing waiting

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.500
A signal arrives — alert, schedule, message, event — and a conversation opens

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.500
The thread it opened, and the agent already working

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.500
The answer — what is wrong, what changed, and what it did not touch

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:33.100
You reply in the thread, and the conversation carries on

6
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.100
What is waiting, and what is stuck — every stalled row names its cause

7
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:46.100
The wiring behind it: where the signal entered, who claimed it, where the answer went

8
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:52.100
Every part of it is a Kubernetes resource — one API, one RBAC model

9
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:59.600
The conversation itself is an object — kubectl, GitOps and RBAC already work
